<p>
If you do a lot of exporting from Org Mode and hate all the rigmarole involved, Charles Choi may have precisely what you need. <a href="http://yummymelon.com/devnull/announcing-burnish.html">He&rsquo;s just released Burnish</a>, an app that largely automates the Org export process. The TL;DR is that when <code>burnish-mode</code> is active and a properly marked Org file is saved, the file is automatically exported and a preview is generated.
</p>
<p>
By default, the app supports exporting to:
</p>
<ul class="org-ul">
<li>HTML</li>
<li>md</li>
<li>odt</li>
<li>info</li>
<li>LaTeX-PDF</li>
</ul>
<p>
but the app is highly configurable and you can add your own export types and export functions. The app comes with a user manual that explains how to do all this.
</p>
<p>
If you only occasionally export Org files, Burnish may be more than you need but if you export a lot of Org files, it may save you some time and effort.</p>
